[size=5][b]SOS Hostile Safeguard[/b][/size]
[size=3][i]v1.0.0 — improved Simple Offence Suppression for temporary "friendly" foes[/i][/size]

[size=4][b]What this fixes[/b][/size]

[b]Simple Offence Suppression[/b] (and especially [b]SOS MCM – Block Friendly Fire[/b]) treats any NPC who is [b]not currently hostile[/b] as a protected friend when you hit them.

That also catches many [b]enemies who are only calm for a moment[/b]:

[list]
[*]Toll / highway bandits after you pay
[*]Arvel the Swift (dragon-claw thief who runs off)
[*]Weylin (Markarth market Forsworn assassin vs Margret) — his base record has [b]zero factions[/b], so faction-only patches miss him
[*]Other quest or modded "talk first" foes who sit in criminal / enemy factions but are not yet hostile
[/list]

Symptoms: surprise attacks do no damage, they never feel like real foes, and no amount of "just hit them harder" works while Block Friendly Fire is on.

This package keeps the original purpose — [b]stray hits on real neutrals and civilians still do not start a war[/b] — but [b]excludes hostile-by-nature actors[/b] so you can kill them properly.

[size=4][b]What this is[/b][/size]

[b]Not a soft side-patch alone.[/b] It is:

[list]
[*][b]Replacement[/b] of powerofthree's [font=courier new]po3_SimpleOffenceSuppression.dll[/font] (same filename; improved fork with exclusions)
[*][b]Addon plugin[/b] (light ESP) with keyword + formlist + a patch to the MCM friendly-fire perk
[*][b]Optional SPID lines[/b] to tag common criminal/enemy factions with the exclusion keyword
[/list]

Disable the original Simple Offence Suppression [b]mod folder[/b] (or ensure this mod wins the DLL path). Keep [b]SOS MCM[/b] enabled.

[size=4][b]How the safeguard works[/b][/size]

Several layers so one framework cannot silently re-protect foes:

[list]
[*][b]DLL[/b] — when SOS would treat a Neutral as a Friend for hit-reaction, skip that for actors in configured hostile factions, with the exclusion keyword, or Very Aggressive / Frenzied (v1.1-style behaviour restored)
[*][b]INI[/b] — [font=courier new]HostileFactions[/font] (faction EditorIDs) and [font=courier new]HostileNPCs[/font] (unique NPC base EditorIDs like [font=courier new]MS01Weylin[/font]); extend without recompiling
[*][b]Keyword + FormList[/b] in the light ESP ([font=courier new]SOS_NoOffenceSuppression[/font], [font=courier new]SOS_HostileFactionList[/font]; formlist can also hold NPC bases)
[*][b]SPID[/b] — tags bandits, warlocks, undead, forsworn, common WE packs, DLC hostiles, plus unique lines for Weylin/Arvel
[*][b]MCM perk patch[/b] — Block Friendly Fire no longer multiplies damage by zero on keyword-tagged hostiles
[/list]

[size=4][b]Requirements[/b][/size]

[b]Hard[/b]
[list]
[*]Skyrim Special Edition / AE with [b]SKSE64[/b]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/32444]Address Library for SKSE Plugins[/url]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/41774]Simple Offence Suppression MCM - Block Friendly Fire[/url] (master of the ESP; the perk this patches)
[/list]

[b]Strongly recommended[/b]
[list]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/36869]Spell Perk Item Distributor (SPID)[/url] — loads the [font=courier new]_DISTR.ini[/font] keyword tags (needed for full MCM damage fix on tagged NPCs)
[/list]

[b]Replaced (do not run stock DLL beside this)[/b]
[list]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/41764]Simple Offence Suppression[/url] by powerofthree — this package ships the improved DLL under the same name. Disable the original SOS mod so only this DLL loads.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Installation[/b][/size]

[list=1]
[*]Install with a mod manager (Vortex / MO2).
[*][b]Disable[/b] the original Simple Offence Suppression (po3) mod folder.
[*][b]Keep[/b] SOS MCM enabled.
[*]Enable this mod. Plugin: [font=courier new]SOS Hostile Safeguard.esp[/font] (light / ESPFE).
[*]Load [b]after[/b] SOS MCM.
[*]Deploy / run the game through SKSE.
[*]Optional check: SKSE log should mention Simple Offence Suppression with Hostile Safeguard exclusions active.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Configuration[/b][/size]

[font=courier new]Data/SKSE/Plugins/po3_SimpleOffenceSuppression.ini[/font]

[code]
[Exclusions]
ExcludeVeryAggressive = true
UseKeywordExclusion = true
ExclusionKeyword = SOS_NoOffenceSuppression
ExclusionFormList = SOS_HostileFactionList
HostileFactions = BanditFaction,BanditAllyFaction,...
HostileNPCs = MS01Weylin,MS13Arvel,e3DemoArvel
[/code]

If a modded quest foe is still protected:
[list]
[*]Add a [b]faction[/b] EditorID to [font=courier new]HostileFactions[/font], and/or
[*]Add the NPC [b]base[/b] EditorID to [font=courier new]HostileNPCs[/font] (required when the actor has no factions, like Weylin)
[/list]
Then restart the game.

[size=4][b]Compatibility[/b][/size]

[list]
[*]Built for SKSE + Address Library (AE 1.6.x path; Address Library version-independent plugin metadata).
[*]ESP is light-flagged; masters Skyrim + SOS MCM.
[*]Does not edit original MCM scripts or redistribute unedited MCM files — only a reviewable perk override in this ESP.
[*]Other SOS "tweaks" that only change the stock INI are unnecessary if you use this package's INI; do not run a second [font=courier new]po3_SimpleOffenceSuppression.dll[/font].
[/list]

[size=4][b]Known notes / testing honesty[/b][/size]

[list]
[*]Structural build and plugin packaging are validated; [b]please report in-game results[/b] for Arvel, toll bandits, and any stubborn quest neutrals.
[*]True civilians, guards, and genuine allies remain protected by design.
[*]SPID absence: DLL faction EditorID list still applies; MCM damage block may still zero damage until the keyword is present (install SPID or tag actors another way).
[/list]

[size=4][b]Uninstall[/b][/size]

Remove this mod, re-enable stock Simple Offence Suppression if desired, keep or remove MCM as you like. No special clean save required for the SPID keyword layer (runtime only).

[size=4][b]Permissions / source[/b][/size]

Upstream Simple Offence Suppression is MIT and allows modification. This release ships a modified DLL and new addon files only — not a reupload of unedited third-party packages.

